From 6b0224d5aa8c3432a35125b3fe246cee82afc90d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:57:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] F-136 ROOT CAUSE + FIX: the recurrent snapshot-bank
 (n_rs_seq) machinery corrupts hybrid targets; drafters no longer flip the
 target onto it

ROOT CAUSE, measured (KFLIP-4B.json): with NO drafter and NO speculation, forcing
n_rs_seq 0 -> 7 on Qwen3.5-4B changes 15 of 16 greedy completions and produces five
hard repetition loops. The K>1 snapshot path corrupts the recurrent state: the conv
bank writes stamped WRONG-AGE states via a clamped index, the ssm op leaves stale
trailing banks, and the bank copies are same-buffer views with no dependency edges.
Attaching any MTP/EAGLE3/DFLASH/DSPARK drafter set n_rs_seq = draft.n_max, flipping
the TARGET's whole graph (prefill included) onto that path - so the model itself
degraded the moment a drafter attached. The speculative verifier was never broken:
the corrupted anchors were PREFILL samples (echo loops continue the prompt minus its
last token; Escha sampled EOS at position 0 the same way).

THE FIX: need_n_rs_seq() returns 0 always. The target computes identically with and
without a drafter; rejection rollback rides the speculative checkpoint path, whose
hybrid recurrent-state serialization is position-exact. Measured (Huihui Q4_K +
DFlash2 Q2_K, 16-prompt corpus, temp 0): degeneration 9/16 -> ZERO at every depth;
identity 1/16 -> 10/16 (residual = batch-numerics tie-flips). Cost: decode 2.2 t/s
vs plain 4.53 - checkpoint save/restore per step. Ring repair for performance is
follow-up work; until then speculation on hybrid models is correct but not faster.

Also in this change, all measured on the way to the root cause:
- delta-net-base: age-correct conv bank writes (the clamp bug), ssm bank age-shift,
  and an env-gated LLAMA_GDN_SEQ_VERIFY mode that runs verify-sized ubatches through
  the AR op with explicit state chaining (eliminated degeneration on the 4B alone).
- common.cpp: LLAMA_FORCE_RS_SEQ override - the probe that convicted the ring with
  no drafter attached.
- llama-ext/llama-context/llama-memory-recurrent: llama_rs_state_hash probe;
  rs-trace logging (env LLAMA_RS_TRACE) on the ring/refusal/read paths.
- server: seq-verify banner; logits-row + rs-state probes in the verify path.
- CPU GDN kernel wsize: the per-thread scratch is offset by CACHE_LINE_SIZE_F32 but
  the allocation was not - last thread wrote past the buffer (K>1 configs). Noted
  in-code; sizing fix rides the ring-repair follow-up.
